BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VINES\, VIEWS & VIBES: HARVEST
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
UID:261010Xjzs8ebhTUu5zIEBBsmM5A
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Harvest in the heart of Sonoma wine country. As gold
 \, amber\, and crimson foliage sweeps across the valley\, the crisp autumn
  air comes alive with the sweet\, unmistakable aroma of crush.\n\nFor one 
 special afternoon\, Chef-Vintner Dustin Valette opens the doors to his Mic
 helin-recognized restaurant\, The Matheson\, and its rooftop lounge\, Roof
  106\, for an extraordinary journey of the senses you won't soon forget.\n
 \nFramed by vibrant Fall foliage and cozy firepits\, this immersive aftern
 oon pairs extraordinary gastronomy with just released Valette wines\, and 
 spellbinding live entertainment from rising star IZZY ESCOBAR\, all in sup
 port of the V Foundation for Cancer Research!\n\nYour VIP Ticket Includes:
 \n\nExclusive Valette Wine: Be among the first to taste these highly covet
 ed\, brand new releases from Valette Wines\, crafted in collaboration with
  a collective of the world’s most celebrated winemakers.\n\nHyper-Season
 al Culinary Pairings: Taste elevated bites curated by award-winning Chef-V
 intner Dustin Valette.\n\nIntimate Set by Izzy Escobar: Experience a rare\
 , up-close performance by the rising soul-pop sensation - hailed by Forbes
  as "Your Pop Queen for 2026" - following show-stopping festival appearanc
 es at BottleRock\, Austin City Limits\, and the Montreal International Jaz
 z Festival.\n\nPremier Silent Auction: Bid on rare wines\, exclusive trave
 l\, music\, sports\, and culinary experiences\, with 100% of auction proce
 eds benefiting The V's goal of Victory Over Cancer.\n\nTake Home Wine for 
 a Cause: Bottles of Valette Wines will be available for purchase\, with 20
 % of proceeds benefiting the V Foundation!\n\nReserve Your Spot Today!\n\n
 To preserve an intimate experience\, tickets are strictly limited and will
  sell out fast! Secure your entry now to immerse yourself in the bounty of
  harvest\, experience powerhouse talent up close\, and make a meaningful i
 mpact.\n\nThe event benefits the V Foundation for Cancer Research\, who si
 nce 1993 has funded over $500 million in game-changing cancer research gra
 nts.
LOCATION:The Matheson
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/vines-views-vibes-harvest-tickets-2002101
 831473
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sing Napa Valley presents “American Songbook Singer Showcase”
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:261008XuBPXseesEaFNaJeA_kaiA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate America’s musical heritage with Sing Napa Valley a
 t the *American Songbook Singer Showcase*. Presented in honor of the Unite
 d States’ 250th anniversary\, this lively afternoon concert travels from
  the 1920s through the early 1960s with jazz standards\, Broadway favorite
 s\, and memorable songs from film. Two concerts: Saturday\, October 24 & S
 unday\, October 25 at 3pm.\n\nWhether these classics are lifelong favorite
 s or brand-new discoveries\, *American Songbook Singer Showcase* promises 
 an uplifting celebration of music’s power to bridge generations and brin
 g people together.\n\nEnjoy timeless music by George and Ira Gershwin\, Co
 le Porter\, Hoagy Carmichael\, and Irving Berlin\, including favorites suc
 h as “Mr. Sandman\,” “Honeysuckle Rose\,” “Night and Day\,” an
 d “Dream a Little Dream of Me.” Sing Napa Valley choir members and spe
 cial guests will take the spotlight in solos\, duets\, trios\, and small e
 nsembles\, joined by collaborative pianist Anthony Mayor. Bring family and
  friends for an uplifting celebration of music that connects generations.
LOCATION:American Legion Hall
URL:http://www.singnapavalley.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bird of Prey Hike at Lynch Canyon
