BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
UID:2609098mzn_Ym4B0C9eYYDTKDGEg
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T163000
UID:26090922R197VRfEOBSTeWLloChw
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Petaluma Cinema Series: The Bride!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T220000
UID:260904qtlVXMYeXEGpbj6OvjR-1w
DESCRIPTION:The Petaluma Cinema Series is a unique educational forum that 
 invites community residents to join Santa Rosa Junior College students to 
 screen and discuss significant classic and modern cinema. Evenings are gen
 erally structured with a 6pm talk or guest interview\, a 7pm screening\, a
 nd a question & answer session following the film. Films are presented in
  4K with 7.1 surround sound. Visit the Petaluma Film Alliance website for 
 complete program details.
LOCATION:Carole L. Elis Auditorium @ SRJC Petaluma
URL:https://petalumafilmalliance.org/2026-fall-schedule/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T160000
UID:260820kBfvEQlIjUWsPqWneSIdGg
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Farmstead at Long Meadow Ranch
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108643274?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
