DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T170000
UID:261020tfnXbizPf0qcD2iF9vb7mw
DESCRIPTION:Richard Turgeon is a San Francisco-based singer/songwriter\, m
 ulti-instrumentalist and record producer. His alternative rock sound has b
 een called "California Rock" or "New Vintage Rock\," is regularly featured
  on SiriusXM\, and has been featured in indie film soundtracks. He's curre
 ntly playing live shows in the Bay Area and beyond with his trio\, RT3.\n\
 nLast year he played drums for national act Donnie Emerson\, subject of th
 e film "Dreamin' Wild\," and Pavement co-founder Scott Kannberg recently s
 hared Rich's cover/video of Pavement's song "Date with IKEA."\n\nHis criti
 cally acclaimed solo records from the last several years have made innumer
 able “best of” lists from various press outlets\, radio stations and b
 loggers from around the world. Visit his website at www.richardturgeon.com
LOCATION:Big Rock Mini Mart & Deli
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108640546?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nathaniel Riley & The Last Revel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T190000
UID:261020ei5AMBOjqUy2STh3KjgvcA
DESCRIPTION:The Last Revel is a four-piece folk group from Minneapolis\, M
 innesota. Utilizing their multi-instrumental abilities\, members Lee Henke
 \, Ryan Acker\,  and Vincenzio Donatelle\, bring a full spectrum of modern
  Americana to life with lush arrangements of three-part vocal harmonies\, 
 acoustic guitar\, upright bass\, fiddle\, and 5-string banjo to consistent
 ly support impassioned performances of their honest and heartfelt songwrit
 ing. Drawing influence from their salt of the earth Midwest ethos the band
 ’s songs so naturally blend the genres of Folk\, Old Time String-Band an
 d Indie Rock to create a sound that echoes the current heartbeat of Americ
 a. \n\nThe Last Revel released their brand new album\, Gone For Good\, pro
 duced by Dave Simonett of Trampled by Turtles on Thirty Tigers on July 18t
 h\, 2025.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108639133?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
