DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T190000
UID:261012_ItIuNN7TEuHEqfvUXTNLg
DESCRIPTION:Matt Jaffe is an indie rock & roll singer/songwriter from San 
 Francisco. Cutting his teeth on countless open mics around the Bay\, Matt 
 started taking music \\(a little bit\\) more seriously when Jerry Harrison
  of Talking Heads offered to produce his first record. Since then\, Matt h
 as continued to churn out more songs than he can remember the words to\, p
 erform on stages throughout the land \\(opening and/or touring with the li
 kes of Mavis Staples\, Wilco\, Bob Weir\, Jackie Greene\, Chuck Prophet\, 
 Melissa Etheridge\, and Blues Traveler\\)\, and collaborate with Tom Higge
 nson of the Plain White T's. Inspired by the likes of Elvis Costello\, Tom
  Petty and Stephin Merritt\, Matt is continuously writing and recording to
  build a songbook that honors his heroes.  Along with serving on Bread & R
 oses Board of Directors\, he is currently rolling out his 7th studio album
 \, Gone Enough to Miss.
LOCATION:Orelar
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108934445?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mdou Moctar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T203000
UID:261012UCf8eldiLUGutYeOC3lXdw
DESCRIPTION:With "Afrique Victime" the prodigious Tuareg guitarist and son
 gwriter rips a new hole in the sky ­– boldly reforging contemporary Sah
 aran music and “rock music” by melding guitar pyrotechnics\, full-blas
 t noise\, and field recordings with poetic meditations on love\, religion\
 , women's rights\, inequality\, and Western Africa’s exploitation at the
  hands of colonial powers.\n\nThe music listeners are the beneficiaries of
  the staggeringly powerful do-it-yourself musical ethic of Mdou Moctar –
  the man and the band – who’ve worked so hard to bring the spirits of 
 families and communities in Niger to the West. Afrique Victime sounds and 
 feels like a Tuareg hand reaching down from the sky\, and we are very luck
 y for this chance to get lifted.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040065192?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T180000
UID:261011iaH21O7QmEWmjzTDDaKpoQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Hotel Healdsburg
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108897113?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
