DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
UID:260910RGhNPklwMECVV9HvpH278g
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Duhon is a songwriter who's weighted\, soulful songs fe
 el like a trustworthy dispatch from the heart of his New Orleans home out 
 to the familiar landmarks of Americana Music.  No Depression call's Duhon 
 "A soulmate of Van Morrison lyrically and vocally."  He tours most commonl
 y as a trio with upright bass and drums.  4 records out thus far\, his 201
 3 album\, "The Moorings\," was nominated for a Grammy\, and he's due to re
 lease a new album in 2024.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108513219?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T163000
UID:260909m3ZUtcKmY0WTlLcJCDbl3w
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweeney Todd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T193000
UID:2609098SctGojf40WplAdGGnKK9Q
DESCRIPTION:Sweeney Todd is largely considered one of Stephen Sondheim’s
  masterpieces. With it\, he aimed to create a musical that could “scare 
 the hell out of everyone\,” and yet\, somehow\, be funny.\n\nThe story c
 enters around Sweeney Todd\, an unjustly exiled barber who returns to Lond
 on\, seeking vengeance against the lecherous judge who framed him and rava
 ged his young wife. The road to revenge leads Todd to Mrs. Lovett\, a reso
 urceful proprietress of a failing pie shop\, above which\, he opens a new 
 barber practice. Mrs. Lovett’s luck sharply shifts when Todd’s thirst 
 for blood inspires the integration of an ingredient into her meat pies tha
 t has the people of 19th Century London lining up…and the carnage has on
 ly just begun!\n\n\\***Content Advisory:** Adult language and violent the
 mes\, as well as controversial pie recipes. Recommended for 12+.\n\nRunnin
 g Time: 2 hours\, 40 minutes including one intermission.\n\nOctober 23rd\,
  24th\, 25th\, \\*29th\, 30th\, 31st\, Nov 1st\, 6th\, 7th\, 8th.\n\nBook 
 by Hugh Wheeler\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Stephen Sondheim\n\nDirected by Ste
 ven David Martin\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Mat
 inee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission:** \n\nA
 dults: $44\n\nStudent w/ID: $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performanc
 e: Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T160000
UID:2609092rZbxrpDHkqn41tpCZcNbQ
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T173000
UID:260831SzWGo5HnWEeCeFIexqqNfg
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween Masquerade Ball: Creatures of the Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T220000
UID:260831QFT3KTy4UUiWgErK00pNEA
DESCRIPTION:As daylight fades\, another world begins to stir.\n\nWe invite
  guests into an evening shaped by shadow and candlelight\, where masks con
 ceal identities\, music fills the darkness\, and the familiar gives way to
  something far more mysterious. Inspired by nocturnal legends\, ancient fo
 lklore\, dark fairy tales\, and the timeless decadence of the masquerade\,
  Creatures of the Night is a celebration of mystery\, transformation\, ele
 gance\, and indulgence.\n\nFor one night\, become something otherworldly.\
 n\nDraw inspiration from the creatures that have haunted stories for centu
 ries: vampires\, witches\, warlocks\, ghouls\, demons\, banshees\, sirens\
 , mermaids\, spiders\, and spectral beings that linger between this world 
 and the next. Perhaps you are a seductive vampire draped in velvet. A sea 
 siren adorned in shimmering scales...\n\nCostumes are encouraged to captur
 e the spirit of the night while embracing the elegance\, drama\, and intri
 gue of a masquerade. Come masked. Come transformed. Come as something thin
 g that only emerges after dark.\n\nIMPORTANT PARKING DETAILS - PLEASE READ
 \n\nDue to Buena Vista's limited parking\, we are offering a limited numbe
 r of ON-SITE VIP Parking Tickets available at $15 per parking space. Avail
 able at checkout as an "ADD-ON" option. For guests not purchasing a VIP Pa
 rking ticket\, you must park Downtown at the Sonoma Plaza or Ridesharing \
 \(Uber or Lyft\\) is encouraged. We will provide Shuttle service at no cha
 rge in front of the Sonoma Mission 114 East Spain Street\, Sonoma\, beginn
 ing at 6:15pm - running every 15 minutes. Downtown parking is available at
  public parking lots\, at no charge. The largest is the Casa Grande lot\, 
 located behind the historic Barracks just north of the Plaza\, with an ent
 rance off First Street East. There are also numerous spaces surrounding th
 e Sonoma Plaza. Private transportation/Ridesharing services are more than 
 welcome to drop off and pick up guests directly at Buena Vista.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160339/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
