BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free Lyft and Cab Rides by Wells Call Injury Lawyers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:261012IwJafeku-UqGrWKFItTchA
DESCRIPTION:According to the Annual Report of California DUI Management In
 formation System\, of the total number of crash fatalities in 2018\, 32.1%
  were alcohol-related in California. We are committed to helping our commu
 nity not be a part of this statistic.\n\nWe pride ourselves on making our 
 community safer and giving back to our neighbors as much as we can. That i
 s why this holiday season\, if you decide to go out and celebrate\, we wil
 l pay for your cab ride home to ensure that you make it home safely.\n\nWe
 ’d like to introduce a new community initiative: Free Lyft and Cab Ride 
 Program to help reduce the number of drunk drivers on the road during the 
 holidays. This holiday season\, if you decide to go and drink\, please mak
 e the responsible choice to grab a ride home instead of getting behind the
  wheel. We will reimburse you for your fare home\, so save that receipt!\n
 \nRead more about our Holiday Ride-Share Program below for full details. 
 \n\nNote: Because of their track record on failing to protect women from s
 exual assault and their lack of regard for consumer rights\, we do not sup
 port Uber.\n\nHow it Works:\n\nThe program is simple. If you have been dri
 nking – take an Lyft or cab\, and you’ll get a reimbursement from us!\
 n\nWe want you home safe this holiday season.\n\nQualifying Holidays:\n\nS
 uper Bowl Sunday\n\nSt. Patrick’s Day\n\nCinco de Mayo\n\nIndependence D
 ay\n\nLabor Day\n\nHalloween\n\nThanksgiving Eve & Day\n\nNew Year’s Eve
  & Day\n\nDetails to the Program:\n\nRide must be on Lyft or a cab \\(Not 
 Uber\\)\n\nRides must be in Solano County\n\nRides must be taken between 5
  pm on the day of the holiday and 10 am the next morning.\n\nYou must be o
 f legal drinking age to qualify \\(21 and over\\).\n\nValid for one\, one-
 way ride to a safe destination.\n\nLimit one reimbursement per household.\
 n\nA maximum value of $25.00 anywhere within Solano County.\n\nThe maximum
  value includes a tip of up to 10%. Anything above a 10% tip on the base f
 are will not be reimbursed.\n\nParticipation in this promotion is limited 
 to the first 25 submissions.\n\nWhen Will I Get My Reimbursement?\n\nWithi
 n 10 business days\, you must submit a copy of your receipt and photo ID v
 ia mail to our office. We will mail you a check for your reimbursement of 
 a qualifying submission within 30 days of the holiday.\n\nWells Call Injur
 y Lawyers 1455 Oliver Rd \\#110 Fairfield\, CA 94534 707-273-1278 www.well
 scall.com/\n\nSubmissions are limited and will fill up fast\, so don’t d
 elay submitting your reimbursement.
LOCATION:CA 94534
URL:https://www.wellscall.com/free-ride-share/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra's American Roots at RanchoNicasio\, CA Nov 1\, Sun
 \, 4:00-6:30
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T181500
UID:261012AwKvCng1dUqzP3ylUqsvEg
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra's American Roots show continues! ...at Rancho 
 Nicasio\, Nicasio\, CA November 1\, Sun\, 4:00-6:30 INDOORS- by the BEST D
 ANCE FLOOR in the North Bay.\n\nIf you don't believe me.. come try it out!
 .. Or.. if you haven't seen the band lately I urge you to come join us... 
 these folks are inspiring!\n\nChoose your Music Service!:\n\nThe album is 
 out: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\n..and the Latest single\, "What Does Your 
 Heart Say?" https://orcd.co/7jjvmmx\n\nLPs\, CDs available all over\, incl
 uding https://www.globerecords.com\n\n1 Old Rancheria Rd Nicasio CA 94946 
 \\(415\\) 662-2219\n\n\\(Free Show\, but reservations recommended\\)\n\nht
 tps://ci.ovationtix.com/35892/production/1290853?performanceId=11867090\n\
 n$15 donation suggested\n\n... w/ Candy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, Luis Rodr
 iguez\, Jen Rund and Mark Larson! ...on resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\,
  telecaster & traps... come on come on!\n\nwe're back on the RootsMuscRepo
 rt charts \\(\\#29 this week\\): https://www.rootsmusicreport.com/charts/v
 iew/album/sub\\_genre/americana-country/weekly/2026-10-03\n\n\\*recent quo
 tes:\n\n"The guitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin traces lines that
  oscillate between melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm section moves fo
 rward with a tranquil groove that never rushes but never falters... Back p
 OrchEstra delivers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human record. An album
  that makes you want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\, and let the st
 ories do their work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine\n\n"...What sets 'Stor
 ies In The Heart' apart is its sense of balance. Resonator guitar\, violin
 \, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro\, and Telecaster create a flexible\, 
 roots-forward palette that allows Back Porchestra to move between styles f
 luidly. The songs echo traditions without reenacting them\, keeping one fo
 ot in the past and the other firmly planted in the present." - Vince's Hot
  Picks \\(Best of 2026\\) New Releases Now\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a compact
  Shelter-in-Place-inspired musical combo ....going back to the basics... F
 ormed for the first time the locked-down summer of 2020. The band draws fr
 om new original material as well as reworked classics by Hank Williams\, T
 aj Mahal\, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles ...eve
 n Christmas Jug Band tunes\n\n... check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video:
  https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun f
 lavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous single\
 , the Neo-Motown/Levon Helm style "Ever Think About It\," is here: https:/
 /orcd.co/qo5579q\n\n"...evokes artists from multiple decades over the last
  century and embraces everything from indie-rock and Americana to Celtic\,
  Motown\, and Western swing. If you need a reference point\, look to bands
  like Dan Hicks and His Hot Licks and Asleep at the Wheel\, whose records 
 also draw on disparate sources." - Jeff Burger\, Americana Highway\n\nmore
  at... https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.
 bandcamp.com\n\nyouTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO
 2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestr
 a.bsky.social\n\nReverb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestr
 a\n\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: http
 s://www.instagram.com/backporchestra/\n\n\\#rootsrock\n\n\\#americanrootsm
 usic\n\n\\#americanamusic\n\n\\#rockabillymusic\n\n\\#twangyguitar\n\n\\#b
 ackporchestra\n\n\\#acousticmusic\n\n\\#adultalbumalternative\n\n\\#singer
 songwriter\n\n\\#folkmusic\n\n\\#folkrock
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
