BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annual Dia de Muertos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T210000
UID:261023pZB7Z6t5PEOvjwJI8jsuXA
DESCRIPTION:November 1\, 2026 at 6 PM\n\nThe Sonoma Community Center will 
 hold its 17th annual Día de Muertos altar lighting on November 1 at 6
 :30 PM at the west side of the SCC Front Garden\, followed by a celebratio
 n with traditional Ballet Folklórico dancers\, food vendors and cultura
 l activities on the SCC Back Patio. Whether they were family\, a dear frie
 nd\, a beloved companion\, or someone whose life touched yours\, their mem
 ory has a place here.  One may also write a personal message on one of t
 he gold paper butterflies provided at the altar\, and hang it alongside t
 he images.\n\nSchedule of Events\n\n**6:30 PM** – Lighting of the Altar\
 n\n**7:00 PM** – Performance by Grupo Folklórico Quetzalen Sonoma\n\n**
 7:30 PM** – Food will be available\n\n**All Night** – Free Face painti
 ng for adults & children\n\nAbout the Altar\n\nOur 12’ public altar\, co
 nstructed by local sculptor Jim Callahan\, has ample room for photos and o
 ther items that honor lost loved ones\, and every year we invite community
  members to contribute their mementos to the ofrenda in a shared celebrati
 on of those who have passed on. See how to submit a photo below. **Communi
 ty members are warmly invited to bring a weather-resistant photograph or 
 image of a departed loved one and hang it on the altar starting Friday\, 
 October 25th.**\n\nDia Programming & Classes\n\nEvery October\, the Center
  offers a variety of programs and other activities in conjunction with Dí
 a de Muertos\, inviting our community to join us in exploring the cultural
  practices and traditions surrounding this holiday. Please check our event
  calendar for more information about upcoming Día de Muertos programming 
 and events.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/events-galleries/dia-de-muertos/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
