DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
UID:261023_0Wol6DAxUC_4Xop_CwbKw
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum! The Napa Valley Museum Yo
 untville has exciting exhibits including John Donohue: All the Restaurants
  of Napa Valley\, a  Mini-Gallery display of the distinctive sketches of 
 the artist John Donohue\, with limited edition prints for sale to benefit 
 the Museum’s arts and education programs.\n\nBank of America Museums on 
 Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on the first full weekend
  of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Bank of America Private B
 ank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is your Bank of America\, M
 errill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and picture ID for access. 
 \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found here: https://about.bank
 ofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-partner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The MAC FREE November 7-8 with Bank of America Museums on Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:2610239qo5jn_kt0uF-hXipg-Jmw
DESCRIPTION:Bank of America cardholders receive free general admission to 
 participating museums nationwide on the first full weekend of each month\;
  this month is November 7-8. \n\nWith Thanksgiving and winter just around
  the corner\, the late fall season means just one thing: it’s the perfec
 t time for some indoor fun at your local museum!  The “MAC” \\(Napa V
 alley Museum of Art & Culture\\) has exciting exhibits including Eames & E
 ames: Meet the Couple Who Defined Modern Design!\, featuring the boundless
  curiosity of Ray and Charles Eames\, two of the 20th century’s most inf
 luential designers. Eames & Eames explores their iterative\, hands-on\, an
 d human-centered approach. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphics
 \, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundbre
 aking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the breadt
 h of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work ope
 ned doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and u
 nderstanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nBank 
 of America Museums on Us program offers FREE weekend general admission on 
 the first full weekend of every month to Bank of America\, Merrill and Ban
 k of America Private Bank credit and debit cardholders. All you need is yo
 ur Bank of America\, Merrill\, or Bank of America Private Bank card and pi
 cture ID for access. \n\nAdditional participating museums can be found he
 re: https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ner
LOCATION:Napa Valley Museum of Art and Culture
URL:https://about.bankofamerica.com/en/making-an-impact/museums-on-us-part
 ners
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
