DESCRIPTION:NRP Certification Class \\(AAP/AHA\\)\n\nThe NRP certification
  class \\(Neonatal Resuscitation Program\\) is developed by the American A
 cademy of Pediatrics \\(AAP\\) in collaboration with the American Heart As
 sociation \\(AHA\\). This Blended Learning class consists of an online cou
 rse followed by an in-person Skills Session with an instructor. American A
 cademy of Pediatrics NRP Provider certifications are issued on the same da
 y.  \n\nLearn from a top-rated\, local CPR training company with over 1\
 ,000 5-star reviews!  Our classes are fun\, engaging\, and expertly taugh
 t by professional first responders.\n\nLEARN MORE and ENROLL: https://vive
 cpr.com/class/heartcode-bls/\n\nCONTACT US: \\(707\\) 612-3277
LOCATION:Vive CPR
URL:https://vivecpr.com/class/nrp-certification/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bill Evans & Chad Manning & Jim Nunally & Max Schwartz & Mike Witc
 her & Sharon Gilchrist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T200000
UID:260914t6VxHSA1aEG8RSbkp1dKIA
DESCRIPTION:“WHO DOES MILES DAVIS\, GREGG ALLMAN\, WILLIE NELSON\, HERBI
 E HANCOCK\, WARREN HAYNES AND DEREK TRUCKS ALL HAVE IN COMMON? BILL EVANS\
 , THAT’S WHO.”\n\nDeeply intrigued and ultimately inspired by American
  roots music\, saxophone legend Bill Evans wrote\, produced and recorded 
 “Soulgrass” in 2005\, garnering a Grammy nod in the process. Soulgrass
  was a breakaway new fusion of jam\, rock\, funk\, roots and jazz\, blendi
 ng the banjo\, fiddle\, mandolin and dobro\, combining the best musicians 
 from Jazz and Americana. Three more CD’s followed in the Soulgrass genre
 \, “The Other Side of Something”\, “Dragonfly”\, and the 2014 rele
 ase of “Live in Moscow” recorded during the first of two sold out U.S.
  State Dept sponsored tours of Russia. Each subsequent release found Bill 
 pushing the musical boundaries of Jazz and Improvisational rock. “Combin
 ing banjo and fiddle with rock guitar became very natural for me in my liv
 e band and recordings. With the addition of vocals\, we were reaching a mu
 ch larger audience of all ages.”\n\nAfter 10 years of touring and breaki
 ng new ground with Soulgrass\, in 2015 Bill introduced the “Bill Evans B
 and”\, a hard hitting montage of Jazz\, Rock\, instrumental and vocals. 
 Evans and drummer Josh Dion are both featured as the new groups lead singe
 rs. The “Bill Evans Band” features Saxophone/vocals\, Guitar/vocals\, 
 bass and drums/vocals with a seamless blend of Jazz\, rock and groove. “
 People really relate to this band. We’re not afraid to play anything. Th
 e Bill Evans Band takes people on a musical journey with jazz\, funk\, and
  rock and roll. For me\, that’s the definition of jazz – Improvisation
  and Exploration that people can still relate to!”\n\n“RISE ABOVE” i
 s Bill’s latest and most accessible release to date \\(2016\\). On this\
 , his 24th solo offering\, Evans explores rich and haunting vocals from sp
 ecial guest singers\, including legend Gregg Allman\, Warren Haynes\, JJ G
 rey\, Anders Osborne\, Murali Coryell\, and Josh Dion. Says Bill\, “This
  recording has been an epic journey. My vision from the beginning was to r
 ecord with some of my favorite singers\, and work on a different song with
  each one of them. The goal was to still make a cohesive and solid perform
 ance out of all this music. It went far beyond my expectations. Sheer plea
 sure start to finish!”\n\n“RISE ABOVE” is tied together with Evans
 ’ pedigree and love of soulful melodies and hard-hitting grooves\, as it
  has been from the very beginning. In addition to his powerhouse guest voc
 alists\, this recording also features: Jake Cinninger \\(Umphrey’s McGee
 \\) and Mike Stern on guitar\, as well as a who’s who among Jazz and Jam
  Band musicians.\n\nEvans is a world-class saxophonist and producer who ma
 de his debut on the international music scene in the 1980s originally with
  Miles Davis\, \\(at the age of 21 years old and recorded 6 records with D
 avis\\) which led to playing with the likes of John McLaughlin\, Herbie Ha
 ncock\, Mick Jagger and Willie Nelson to name a few. With 24 solo albums\,
  Grammy nods\, and countless collaborations and tours\, Evans has continue
 d to explore a dazzling variety of adventurous musical settings as a pione
 ering bandleader\, consistently winning fans in the worldwide arena. RECEN
 T HIGHLIGHTS include touring and/or performing with his own Bill Evans Ban
 d as well as Warren Haynes\, Robben Ford \\(Soulgrass meets Blues\\)\, Phi
 l Lesh & Friends\, The Stern/Evans Band\, Medeski Martin & Wood\, and coun
 tless sit-ins with The Allman Brothers Band\, Umphrey’s Mcgee\, Moe\, Bl
 ues Traveler\, Galactic and more. Evans will be spending much of his time 
 touring with the Bill Evans Band in support of his new album “Rise Above
 ”.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039739283?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Careless Whisper
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T190000
UID:2609106dXIfHz7SUalUlNOnFgKYQ
DESCRIPTION:Welcome Spandex Rebellion that is Careless Whisper\, The 1980s
  Live.\n\nCareless Whisper brings the MTV and Sunset Strip ’80s party to
  life with high-energy hits\, wild costumes\, rad choreography\, and nonst
 op audience participation. \n\nWith a glam rock aesthetic and a setlist pa
 cked with the decade’s biggest anthems\, every show is a neon-soaked tri
 p back to the most fun era in music.\n\nWhether it's the iconic tunes of G
 eorge Michael and Bon Jovi\, the dance-pop anthems of Whitney Houston\, or
  the rock ballads of Journey\, Careless Whisper transports back to feeling
  alive in 1985 with an endless 80s playlist.\n\nRelive the 80s\, LIVE with
  Careless Whisper.
LOCATION:The Penngrove Pub
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108744570?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T163000
UID:260909q9NBSM6lPEWWg6KmQx-KrQ
DESCRIPTION:September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month. On Monday\, 
 Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person Senio
 r Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\, CA.
  The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.-4:3
 0 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming native 
 artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in the
 ir art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts. The
  artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, guest cur
 ator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·  
        Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\, cu
 ltural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry Edwar
 d Frank\, Yurok/Kashaya Pomo\, who will show paintings and work with Legos
  titled Mind Prison\,\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas \\(Nico
 \\) Vargas\, Kashia Band of Pomo Indians\, whose art was featured at the 5
 5th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carretero\; 
 Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\, Kash
 ia Band of Pomo Indians\; Angelica Smith\, Manchester Point Arena and Yoka
 yo Rancheria\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\, Kashia Ba
 nd of Pomo Indians\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaugh\; Katie Wi
 lliams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, Big Valley Pomo Tribe.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sacred Sounds Sessions: Arctic Beats with Snow Raven
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T210000
UID:2607152w1x3A19ZkKJLsN09SZKUQ
DESCRIPTION:with Snow Raven\n\nFollow the rhythms back to yourself.\n\nRoo
 ted in the ancient wisdom of the Sakha people and the living pulse of the 
 Arctic world\, Snow Raven weaves sacred vocal traditions with deep bass\, 
 hypnotic rhythms\, and immersive live looping into a one-of-a-kind sonic c
 eremony.\n\nJourney inward through:\n\nThe *khomus* (Sakha mouth harp)
 —trance-inducing vibration that stills the mind\n\nBird & animal calls t
 hat reawaken your wild\, instinctual self\n\nEthereal shamanic singing tha
 t bridges seen and unseen worlds\n\nArctic-inspired beats that move body a
 nd soul\n\nThis is more than a concert—it’s a ceremony in sound. Come 
 ready to dance\, drop in\, and remember who you are through the rhythms of
  the natural world.\n\nCommunity song. Sacred dance. Ancient sound. Modern
  floor.\n\nBring a picnic: Gates will open two hours before the performanc
 e.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/sacred-sounds-sessions
 -arctic-beats-with-snow-raven-sr1e26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
