BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Veterans Holiday Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T160000
UID:260930hKh4_DlDEEeaoWG7SCcAvg
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 will host its 4th Annual Ve
 terans Holiday Market on Saturday\, November 14\, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\,
  and Sunday\, November 15\, from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. at the Veterans Memoria
 l Building\, 126 First St. West\, Sonoma.\n\nThe two-day holiday market wi
 ll feature one-of-a-kind\, limited-edition goods handcrafted by local arti
 sts and makers. With several vendors participating\, shoppers will have an
  opportunity to find unique gifts while supporting the Auxiliary’s missi
 on of helping those who have served and their loved ones.\n\nThe Native Da
 ughters of the Golden West\, Sonoma Parlor No. 209\, will also host a spec
 ial community activity\, “Make a Veteran a Christmas Card.” Community 
 members of all ages are invited to create handmade holiday cards that will
  be delivered to area veterans living in assisted living facilities and nu
 rsing homes.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is free and open to the public
 \, with a special invitation extended to military members\, veterans and t
 heir families. Proceeds from the event will help provide assistance to vet
 erans and military families who are experiencing hardship.\n\nThe VFW Auxi
 liary is an all-volunteer service organization whose members include the s
 pouses\, parents\, grandparents\, brothers\, sisters and other family memb
 ers of those who have served in overseas combat. Since 1934\, members of S
 onoma VFW Auxiliary Post 1943 have worked to support those who have served
  and strengthen the community around them.\n\nThe Auxiliary’s community 
 service efforts have included toy and monetary donations to Toys for Tots\
 , Christmas gifts and cards for veterans at the Yountville Veterans Home\,
  as well as clothing and food drives benefiting local emergency service or
 ganizations.\n\nThe Veterans Holiday Market is an opportunity for the enti
 re community to come together during the holiday season—not only to shop
  and celebrate\, but also to show appreciation for those who have served a
 nd to remind veterans and their loved ones that they are valued\, remember
 ed and not alone.\n\nVeteran Families Helping Veterans\n\nFor more informa
 tion contact: Debbie Chandler \\(707\\)364-2734
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Building
URL:http://vfwpost1943.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Western Swing Night with The Dogweeds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T220000
UID:260929b2UJEJD0ykmohgEvpwUUbQ
DESCRIPTION:Get on your cowboy boots\, grab your honey and come out to the
  Napa Grange for a great evening of Western Swing with The Dogweeds!\n\nDB
  Productions and the Welcome Grange bring another great evening of live mu
 sic to Napa. The Dogweeds draw inspiration from the Western Swing dance ba
 nds of the 1930's and 40's\, but with a modern take. Blazing instrumentals
  and honest\, soulful vocal harmonies meet dance-inspiring grooves in a so
 und that is both unique and familiar. Genre bending originals add elements
  of jazz\, blues\, vintage pop and folk\, while dazzling new arrangements 
 bring old classics and deep cuts to life.\n\n"*Lyrics to make you think\, 
 but music to make you move... "* Rachel Cholst\, Adobe and Teardrops\n\n"*
 red-hot musicianship and a genuine love for Western Swing - proof that the
  genre thrives in the hands of the next generation."* Mae McCoy\, Western 
 Swing Society
LOCATION:Napa Welcome Grange
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/western-swing-dance-concert-with-the-dogw
 eeds-tickets-1999737350246?aff=oddtdtcreator#location
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Echoes of Innocence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T213000
UID:2609295HnCSidAx0KLKvv-qE2Ksw
DESCRIPTION:Echoes of Innocence\n\nNovember 14\, 15 & 16\, 2026\n\nWeill H
 all\, Green Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong\,** conductor\n\n**Oli
 ver Herbert\,** cello\n\n**Elisa Sunshine\,** soprano\n\n**SERGEI RACHMANI
 NOFF:** *Vocalise* in E minor for Soprano and Orchestra\, Opus 34\, No. 14
  **CAMILLE SAINT-SAËNS:** Concerto No. 1 in A minor for Cello and Orchest
 ra\, Opus 33 **GUSTAV MAHLER:** Symphony No. 4 in G major for Soprano and 
 Orchestra\n\nRachmaninoff’s *Vocalise* is a landmark piece of wordless l
 onging and quiet intensity. Bay Area native Oliver Herbert performs Saint-
 Saëns’ Cello Concerto No. 1\, a work that unfolds in a single continuou
 s movement\, shifting seamlessly between urgency and repose. Closing the p
 erformance\, Mahler’s ethereal Symphony No. 4 features a soprano in its 
 final movement\, which delivers a radiant and transcendent ending.\n\n**Pr
 ograms\, artists\, dates\, and prices are subject to change without notice
 . Tickets are subject to availability. All Tickets are nonrefundable.**\n\
 nPhoto by Todd Rosenberg
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/echoes-of-innocence/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
