BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artazan Handcraft Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261021Y7BKSxuaOUSYzzQ7Eo7BSg
DESCRIPTION:Artazan Handcraft Market returns to Pasadena November 14–15\
 , bringing together artists\, artisans\, craftspeople and the community fo
 r a weekend celebrating creativity and work made by hand.\n\nInspired by t
 he ideas behind the Arts & Crafts movement\, the handcraft market celebrat
 es creativity\, thoughtful design\, skilled work and the people behind the
  things we bring into our lives. That spirit is reflected in a contemporar
 y and wide-ranging mix of handcraft\, encompassing many different material
 s\, traditions and creative approaches.\n\nHeld at the Pasadena Convention
  Center\, the two-day market will be filled with work from independent art
 ists and artisans across an eclectic mix of mediums. Visitors might discov
 er jewelry and metalsmithing\, ceramics and glass\, crochet and fiber art\
 , woodworking and handcrafted clocks\, painting and mixed media\, wearable
  art\, leatherwork\, home décor\, artisan foods and much more. From time-
 honored skills to unexpected new ideas\, the market reflects the remarkabl
 e variety of what people are creating by hand today.\n\nThe weekend will a
 lso connect with Pasadena’s broader creative community\, bringing togeth
 er local and regional artists\, arts organizations\, educators and visitor
 s. Guests can talk directly with artists\, learn about their materials and
  techniques\, take part in hands-on workshops\, watch demonstrations and e
 njoy live music throughout the weekend.\n\nTaking place at the beginning o
 f the holiday season\, the November market offers an alternative to mass-p
 roduced holiday shopping\, with distinctive gifts\, original art\, artisan
  foods and objects for the home\, while directly supporting independent ar
 tists and small creative businesses.\n\nMore than a place to shop\, Artaza
 n offers an opportunity to see handcraft up close\, discover something une
 xpected and experience the incredible range of things being made by hand t
 oday.\n\nEVENT DETAILS Artazan Handcraft Market November 14–15\, 2026 Pa
 sadena Convention Center • Pasadena\, California Saturday & Sunday • 1
 0 a.m.–5 p.m.\n\nTickets\, workshops\, exhibitor information and additio
 nal details are available at Artazan.com.
LOCATION:Pasadena Convention Center
URL:https://www.artazan.com/pasadena.php
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jim Lauderdale
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T150000
UID:261020kBWWUaoHz0W9mh3CxXJ0pw
DESCRIPTION:Two-time Grammy-winning singer and master songwriter Jim Laude
 rdale is both a "songwriter's songwriter\," who's written/co-written many 
 modern classics for iconic artists\, as well as an intuitive sideman\, who
 's enhanced the music of a bevy of esteemed musicians. As a solo artist\, 
 since 1986 up until now\, he's created a bodywork spanning 37 albums of im
 aginative roots music\, encompassing all that is today’s musical landsca
 pe. His combination of Country\, Bluegrass\, Soul\, R&B and Rock has helpe
 d to pave the way for the current Americana movement.\n\nFor several decad
 es\, Jim has written songs for and worked with some of the finest artists 
 in traditional and modern music including Ralph Stanley\, Elvis Costello\,
  George Strait\, Buddy Miller\, Lucinda Williams\, John Oates\, Solomon Bu
 rke\, Lee Ann Womack\, Old Crow Medicine Show\, Mary Chapin Carpenter\, Bl
 ake Shelton\, the Dixie Chicks\, Vince Gill\, Patty Loveless\, and Gary Al
 lan among others.\n\nLauderdale co-hosts "The Buddy & Jim Show" weekly rad
 io program on SiriusXM with Buddy Miller. Recently\, the Americana Music A
 ssociation honoured him with the WagonMaster Lifetime Achievement Award. J
 im has certainly earned it\, having released a staggering 37 albums with t
 he latest My Favorite Place out June 21st on Sky Crunch Records 2024. \n\n
 Whether solo or band\, Jim Lauderdale a triple threat performer\, songwrit
 er and musician who is constantly reinventing himself!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern Novato
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108940639?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author's Afternoon with Marlo Faulkner on "The Second Mrs. London"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T153000
UID:2610193g6Gr-7JzU6pD47uZfdh-Q
DESCRIPTION:Step into the world of Charmian Kittredge London with author M
 arlo Faulkner as she presents her book\, “The Second Mrs. London."\n\nA 
 native of Coeur d’Alene\, Idaho\, Marlo Faulkner has led a remarkable an
 d adventurous life\, working as a roadie\, English instructor\, columnist\
 , literary scholar\, and a featured speaker for the Jack London Society. H
 er fascination with Charmian London began during a visit to Jack London St
 ate Historic Park\, where she discovered Charmian’s private apartment. Y
 ears of research\, travel\, and study culminated in her new novel\, “The
  Second Mrs. London\,” bringing to life the extraordinary story of one o
 f Sonoma Valley’s most captivating women.\n\nSet in San Francisco at the
  turn of the 20th century\, the novel tells the story of Charmian\, a bold
  and ambitious woman whose life is forever changed when she meets young wr
 iter Jack London. From a broken picnic date to a devoted partnership as fr
 iend\, confidante\, editor\, and companion. Their story is one of passion\
 , resilience\, and determination.\n\nFaulkner will share details of the re
 markable life of Charmian London\, read excerpts from her book inspired by
  this extraordinary woman\, and sign copies for attendees.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/the-second-mrs-london-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard Heinberg: A Celebration of His Life and Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261018VKuFOjt3C0OOEdt0k-jB0g
DESCRIPTION:***Author • Musician • Senior Fellow at Post Carbon Instit
 ute • Environmental Educator • Artist • Husband • Friend***\n\nYou
  are warmly invited to join family\, friends\, colleagues\, and admirers f
 rom around the world on **November 15th** as we come together to celebrate
  the extraordinary life and legacy of **Richard Heinberg**.\n\nA Senior Fe
 llow at Post Carbon Institute for nearly 20 years\, Richard was a pioneeri
 ng voice on resilience and the energy crisis. He was the author of fourtee
 n books\, hundreds of articles\, and the award-winning monthly *Museletter
 .*\n\nRichard was a skilled writer and speaker who could synthesize comple
 x issues and ideas into understandable language. His calm demeanor\, sharp
  wit\, and intense focus made difficult and daunting facts feel bearable.\
 n\nRichard was a lifelong violinist and guitarist who\, more recently\, to
 ok up the piano. For decades\, he maintained a devoted\, focused daily pra
 ctice and played in bands\, chamber groups\, duos\, and orchestras through
 out his life.\n\nBeyond his public work\, those who knew him personally we
 re struck by his genuine curiosity. He was always asking questions and tru
 ly listening for the answers.  \n\nJoin us in Santa Rosa on November 15th
  for an afternoon of gratitude and celebration for a life so fully and gen
 erously lived. Richard’s commemoration will be held from 2:30 to 4:00 pm
 \, with arrival starting at 2:00 pm and a social hour to follow the progra
 m.\n\nSeating is limited. Please use the RSVP link on EverLoved to save yo
 ur spot.
LOCATION:See EverLoved for venue information
URL:https://everloved.com/life-of/richard-heinberg/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yototl de Healdsburg 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261115T170000
UID:261017a1Gai1Js5km4IxZ4r8N_rw
DESCRIPTION:Ballet Folklórico Comunitario Yolotl brings a captivating dis
 play of bright costumes\, swirling skirts\, and cultural comunitario to th
 e Raven Theater!\n\n“Yolotl“ means ”heart“ in Nahuatl. The languag
 e\, which is part of a group of languages in the Uto-Aztecan language fami
 ly\, is spoken by millions of people in central Mexico and in smaller popu
 lations in the United States. Experience the heart of Mexico and it’s ma
 ny regions and cultures with the beauty of Ballet Folklórico Comunitario 
 Yolotl\, a cadre of about 55 dancers formed under the direction of “maes
 tra” Yolanda Girón.\n\nSunday\, Nov. 15th\, at 5:00 PM. Doors open 4:00
  PM.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/yolotl-de-healdsburg/?eventstart=17947
 90800&eventend=1794798000&timezone=America%2FLos_Angeles
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
